WEBVTT

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday, fourth of March. Are we all on?</v>

00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:12.919
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, hang on, it's picked the laptop mic again.</v>

00:00:13.609 --> 00:00:19.210
<v Priya Raman>We can hear you. Bit like you're inside a biscuit tin, but we can hear you.</v>

00:00:20.929 --> 00:00:24.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Before we start, the football last night. Honestly, what was that?</v>

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.690
<v Callum Reid>Not a conversation I need before I've finished this tea.</v>

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:35.700
<v Jamie Brennan>He's been remarkably quiet about football this morning, actually.</v>

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:40.929
<v Sarah Okafor>Ha. Right, we'll spare him. Quick updates first, then today's bits.</v>

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>There. Headset now. Less biscuit tin?</v>

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Much better. Jamie, go on.</v>

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:51.179
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah so, shift handover report's gone round. All fine with that.</v>

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.369
<v Hannah Price>Lovely, thanks.</v>

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:01.369
<v Jamie Brennan>And Reidy asked me to pass on that the pre-use checks on the trucks are all done.</v>

00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:05.209
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Jamie. Saves me shouting over this lot.</v>

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.790
<v Jamie Brennan>Last one from me: I've finished recalibrating the sensors on the pop valve. That's sorted.</v>

00:01:11.379 --> 00:01:12.579
<v Priya Raman>Nice one.</v>

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.530
<v Sarah Okafor>My function test on the relief valve is done as well.</v>

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:19.870
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good, yeah.</v>

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:27.209
<v Sarah Okafor>And I've done the site visit at Kestrel with the contractor. Boxed that off.</v>

00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:28.920
<v Callum Reid>Right, lovely.</v>

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.420
<v Sarah Okafor>Reidy, how are you getting on with the near-miss write-up?</v>

00:01:34.849 --> 00:01:43.599
<v Callum Reid>The near miss at Injection Moulding Line 1, yeah. Made a start on it. I've got the opening bit down, but there's more to write.</v>

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.099
<v Hannah Price>Okay, thanks.</v>

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:54.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Oh, and I signed off the inspection on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing on Tuesday. That's already done.</v>

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.650
<v Hannah Price>Yep, understood.</v>

00:01:59.579 --> 00:02:08.330
<v Sarah Okafor>Just an observation as well: I saw the pressure on the Line 3 Chiller dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:09.419 --> 00:02:10.819
<v Tomasz Nowak>Without anyone touching anything?</v>

00:02:12.219 --> 00:02:18.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, no adjustment. Back where it was. Just mentioning what I saw, nothing I'm handing out off that.</v>

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.219
<v Priya Raman>Right, got you.</v>

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:28.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, today's work. Three things, and there's a definite order to the production one.</v>

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.099
<v Callum Reid>Yep. Sorry if there's a racket my end, I'm by the door.</v>

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:44.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Reidy, can you go to the hydraulics lot to pick up the replacement parts for the wrapper by 11am? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:54.289
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll go to the hydraulics lot and pick up the replacement parts for the wrapper by 11am. First thing for me.</v>

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.949
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, makes sense. No parts, no running.</v>

00:02:59.669 --> 00:03:01.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. That collection takes precedence, Reidy.</v>

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.610
<v Callum Reid>Understood. That one first.</v>

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:13.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the big board today? That's fairly important.</v>

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:18.469
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the big board today.</v>

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.550
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, I was going to speak—no, carry on.</v>

00:03:24.009 --> 00:03:29.259
<v Priya Raman>Only saying, I've got both bits, the permit and the isolation. Not just the paperwork.</v>

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's what I meant. Thanks.</v>

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:42.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Then Reidy, if you've got a spare minute, can you do a site visit at the warehouse with the contractor?</v>

00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:52.460
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll do the site visit at the warehouse with the contractor if I've got a spare minute. Collection comes first, though.</v>

00:03:54.740 --> 00:04:00.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. The warehouse visit is the spare-minute one, not something to squeeze ahead of the parts.</v>

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.530
<v Hannah Price>At least the priorities are clear.</v>

00:04:05.479 --> 00:04:08.979
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. No trying to be in two places at once.</v>

00:04:09.889 --> 00:04:13.389
<v Tomasz Nowak>Teams makes it look possible. Factory's a bit less forgiving.</v>

00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:17.269
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Any questions on what we've agreed?</v>

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.259
<v Hannah Price>Nothing from me.</v>

00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:22.220
<v Jamie Brennan>No, all clear here.</v>

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.449
<v Priya Raman>Same, yeah.</v>

00:04:25.839 --> 00:04:28.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. We'll leave it there. Cheers, everyone.</v>

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.930
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. And no more football chat, please.</v>
